IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rp-dates`
IMPORT `rp-rules`

-- Supreme Court Civil Procedure Act 1932 (Tas), Part VII -- the questions of the PERSON WITH A CLAIM in a representative
-- proceeding (class action) in the Supreme Court of Tasmania.
--
-- SEAT: an individual with a claim against a defendant who either brings the class action (the representative party) or
-- is one of the group on whose behalf it is brought (a group member). "Can I start a class action?", "Am I in the group
-- without agreeing?", "By when can I opt out?", "Can I be made to pay costs?", "Must I be told of a settlement?", "Am I
-- bound by the judgment?", "Is my claim on the fund in time?", "Can I appeal if the representative party does not?",
-- "Is my limitation period running, and by when must I sue on my own?". The Court gets no seat: its satisfactions,
-- leave, orders and approvals are asked as facts. The defendant's seat is not written (NOTES.md).
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of rp-rules.l4.
-- No question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (CC BY 4.0, State of Tasmania). For the
-- latest information on Tasmanian Government legislation please go to www.legislation.tas.gov.au. Unofficial copy; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Supreme Court Civil Procedure Act 1932 (Tas), Part VII: the claimant's questions`

§§ `Bringing a class action`

@export Does Part VII (representative proceedings, class actions) of the Supreme Court Civil Procedure Act 1932 (Tas) apply to the proceeding (ss 64, 65)? It applies to civil proceedings in the Supreme Court of Tasmania commenced from 9 September 2019, whenever the cause of action arose; not to criminal proceedings or proceedings in another court.
GIVEN `kind` IS A `Kind of proceeding` @desc What kind of proceeding it is: a civil proceeding in the Supreme Court of Tasmania; a criminal proceeding; or a proceeding in another court
      `commenced` IS A DATE @desc The date the proceeding was (or will be) commenced
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the class action law apply` MEANS
    `ss 64, 65 -- Part VII applies to the proceeding` `kind` `commenced`

@export Can I start a class action (representative proceeding) in the Supreme Court of Tasmania on behalf of others with claims like mine (ss 66(1), 67(1))? Yes if 7 or more persons (you included) have claims against the same defendant, the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances, they give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact, and you have a claim against that defendant yourself. The kind of relief does not matter (s 66(2)).
GIVEN `kind` IS A `Kind of proceeding` @desc What kind of proceeding it would be: a civil proceeding in the Supreme Court of Tasmania; a criminal proceeding; or a proceeding in another court
      `commenced` IS A DATE @desc The date you would commence it
      `persons` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons, including you, have claims against the same defendant
      `my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a claim against that defendant yourself (standing to sue them on your own behalf)
      `circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all the claims are in respect of, or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances
      `common question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all the claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I start a class action` MEANS
    `ss 66(1), 67(1) -- I may commence a representative proceeding` (`ss 64, 65 -- Part VII applies to the proceeding` `kind` `commenced`) `persons` `my claim` `circumstances` `common question`

@export I started the class action but no longer have a claim of my own (for example I settled it): can I still carry on the proceeding and appeal (s 67(3))? Yes: a person who commenced representative proceedings keeps standing to continue them and to appeal even if they cease to have a claim against any defendant.
GIVEN `commenced it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person who commenced the representative proceeding
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I carry on although my own claim has ended` MEANS
    `s 67(3) -- I keep standing to continue and to appeal` `commenced it`

§§ `Being in the group`

@export Am I a group member in the class action even though I never agreed to join (ss 64, 68)? Consent is not needed if you fall within the group the originating process describes; but the Commonwealth, a State or Territory, a Minister, a public-purpose statutory body, or an officer acting as such, is a group member only with written consent.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who I am, for s 68` @desc Who you are: an individual, company or other private body; an officer of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory acting in that capacity; a Minister; the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or a public-purpose body corporate established by law (not an incorporated company or association)
      `within` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you fall within the group as the originating process (or a document filed with it) describes or identifies it
      `consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given written consent to be a group member
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a group member` MEANS
    `ss 64, 68 -- I am a group member` `who` `within` `consented`

@export I am under a legal incapacity: can I be a group member, and who can take steps in the class action for me (s 69)? You need no substitute decision-maker merely to be a group member, but you can take a step or conduct part of the proceeding only through your substitute decision-maker (a person with a legal right or obligation to make decisions for you).
GIVEN `incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a person under a legal incapacity
      `by decision-maker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the step in question is being taken by your substitute decision-maker
GIVETH A `Group member under a legal incapacity`
`Can a step be taken for me under incapacity` MEANS
    `s 69 -- a group member under a legal incapacity` `incapacity` `by decision-maker`

§§ `Opting out`

-- Arises once a class action that includes you has begun.

@export What is the last day on which I can give notice opting out of the class action (s 71(2))? Notice must be written and given before the date the Court fixes (or a later date it fixes on application), so the last day is the day before that date.
GIVEN `opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court fixed (or, if extended, the later date it fixed) before which group members may opt out
GIVETH A DATE
`Last day to opt out` MEANS
    `s 71(2) -- the last day to give an opt-out notice` `opt-out date`

@export Have I opted out of the class action, or can I still (s 71)? A group member opts out by written notice given before the date the Court fixes; once that date arrives only the Court can fix a later one, on application by a group member, the representative party or the defendant.
GIVEN `commenced` IS A DATE @desc The date the class action was commenced
      `opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court fixed (or, if extended, the later date) before which group members may opt out
      `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given a written notice opting out (a notice not in writing does not count)
      `given on` IS A DATE @desc The date you gave the written notice (if you have not, any date: it is not used)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where my opting out stands`
`Have I opted out` MEANS
    `s 71 -- where my opting out stands` `commenced` `opt-out date` `notice given` `given on` `today`

@export Can the hearing of the class action begin on this day, before I have had the whole opt-out period (s 71(4))? The hearing must not begin earlier than the date fixed for opting out, except with the Court's leave.
GIVEN `opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc The date fixed before which group members may opt out
      `hearing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the hearing begins (or is to begin)
      `leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has given leave for the hearing to begin earlier
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the hearing begin then` MEANS
    `s 71(4) -- the hearing may begin on that day` `opt-out date` `hearing day` `leave`

@export My claim arose after the class action began: can the group be altered to include me (s 72)? On the representative party's application the Court may give leave to amend the group description to include a person whose cause of action accrued after the class action began but before a date the Court fixes, and who would otherwise have been in the group.
GIVEN `commenced` IS A DATE @desc The date the class action was commenced
      `accrued` IS A DATE @desc The date your cause of action accrued
      `cut-off` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court fixes when giving leave (your cause of action must have accrued before it)
      `would have been included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would have been in the group (or would have been with your consent) had your cause of action accrued before the class action began
      `leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court gives leave to amend the group description
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be added to the group` MEANS
    `s 72 -- the group may be altered to include me` `commenced` `accrued` `cut-off` `would have been included` `leave`

§§ `If the Court stops the class action`

@export Can the Court order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action (ss 73, 74, 75)? Yes if it appears likely there are fewer than 7 group members; or, on the defendant's application where money is claimed for group members, the cost of identifying them and distributing would be excessive; or the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice because of a ground in s 75(1). Not merely because the group leaves people out or is aggregated for litigation funding (s 75(2)).
GIVEN `fewer than 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears likely to the Court that there are fewer than 7 group members
      `money claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relief claimed is or includes payment of money to group members (other than costs)
      `distribution excessive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the defendant's application, the Court concludes the defendant's cost of identifying group members and distributing would likely be excessive having regard to the likely total
      `ground` IS A `Section 75 ground` @desc The s 75(1) ground relied on, if any: (a) costs higher than separate proceedings; (b) the relief can be had another way; (c) not efficient and effective; (d) the representative party cannot adequately represent the group; (e) otherwise inappropriate; only that the group omits people or is aggregated for litigation funding; or none
      `interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice to stop it because of that ground
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the class action be stopped` MEANS
    `ss 73-75 -- the Court may order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action` `fewer than 7` `money claimed` `distribution excessive` `ground` `interests of justice`

@export The Court has ordered that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action: what happens to my claim (s 76)? The representative party may continue the proceeding on their own behalf; a group member may apply to be joined as a plaintiff, and the Court may order it.
GIVEN `role` IS A `My role` @desc Your role: the representative party; or a group member (not the representative party)
      `order made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered under s 73, 74 or 75 that the proceeding no longer continue under Part VII
GIVETH A `After an order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action`
`What happens to my claim if the class action is stopped` MEANS
    `s 76 -- what follows an order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action` `role` `order made`

§§ `Costs`

@export Can I be ordered to pay costs in the class action (ss 78(2), 89A)? A group member who is not the representative party cannot be ordered to pay costs, except the costs of a question about their own claim that they were permitted to appear for (s 78), or as s 77 authorises.
GIVEN `role` IS A `My role` @desc Your role: the representative party; or a group member (not the representative party)
      `costs` IS A `The costs in question` @desc Which costs: of a question relating only to your claim that the Court permitted you to appear for (s 78); connected with a sub-group under s 77; or any other costs of the proceeding
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be ordered to pay costs` MEANS
    `ss 78(2), 89A -- costs may be awarded against me` `role` `costs`

@export As representative party, can the Court order that my costs beyond what I can recover from the defendant be paid to me out of the damages (s 89D)? If the Court has awarded damages and is satisfied your reasonably incurred costs are likely to exceed the costs you can recover from the defendant, it may order the whole or part of the excess paid to you from the damages.
GIVEN `representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are or have been the representative party or a sub-group representative party
      `damages awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made an award of damages in the class action
      `satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied your reasonably incurred costs are likely to exceed the costs you can recover from the defendant
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my excess costs come out of the damages` MEANS
    `s 89D -- the Court may order the excess of my costs paid out of the damages` `representative` `damages awarded` `satisfied`

§§ `The representative party`

@export Can the Court replace the representative party (or a sub-group representative party) on my application (ss 80, 83(3))? On a group member's application, if it appears to the Court they cannot adequately represent the group, or the representative party has sought leave to withdraw; for a sub-group representative party, on a sub-group member's application if they cannot adequately represent the sub-group.
GIVEN `whom` IS A `Whom I want replaced` @desc Whom you want replaced: the representative party; or the sub-group representative party
      `sub-group member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of that sub-group (needed only for a sub-group representative party)
      `inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the Court that they cannot adequately represent the interests of the members
      `withdrawing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the representative party has sought leave to withdraw after settling, or while seeking leave to settle, their own claim
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the representative party be replaced` MEANS
    `ss 80, 83(3) -- the Court may substitute another on my application` `whom` `sub-group member` `inadequate` `withdrawing`

@export As representative party, can I settle my own claim, or withdraw as representative party (s 83)? Both need the Court's leave; withdrawal is only for a representative party settling their own claim, and the Court cannot give leave until group members have had notice in time to seek a substitute and any substitution application is decided.
GIVEN `what` IS A `What I want to do as representative party` @desc What you want to do: settle your own claim; or withdraw as representative party
      `settling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are seeking leave to settle, or have settled, your own claim
      `notice in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether notice of your withdrawal application was given to group members under s 84(1) in time for them to apply for a substitute
      `substitution decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every application to substitute another representative party has been determined
      `leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court gives leave
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I settle or withdraw as representative party` MEANS
    `s 83 -- I may do this as representative party` `what` `settling` `notice in time` `substitution decided` `leave`

§§ `Settlement, notices and stays`

@export Can the class action be settled or discontinued (s 82(1))? Only with the Court's approval.
GIVEN `approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has approved the settlement or discontinuance
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the class action be settled` MEANS
    `s 82(1) -- the class action may be settled or discontinued` `approved`

@export Can the Court decide whether to approve the settlement before group members have been told of it (s 82(3))? Not unless notice has been given to group members under s 84, or the Court is satisfied it is just to decide without it.
GIVEN `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether notice of the settlement approval application has been given to group members under s 84
      `just` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied it is just to decide the application without that notice
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the settlement approval be decided` MEANS
    `s 82(3) -- the settlement approval application may be decided` `notice given` `just`

@export Must I, as a group member, be given notice of this matter (s 84)? Notice must be given of the start of the class action and the right to opt out, an application to dismiss for want of prosecution, an application to approve a settlement, and the representative party's application to withdraw, unless the Court dispenses with it where no damages are claimed; of money paid into Court if the Court orders; and of any other matter the Court orders. Notice is due as soon as practicable.
GIVEN `matter` IS A `The matter` @desc The matter: the start of the proceeding and your right to opt out; the defendant's application to dismiss for want of prosecution; an application to approve a settlement; the representative party's application to withdraw; money paid into Court; or some other matter
      `damages claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relief sought in the class action includes any claim for damages
      `dispensed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has dispensed with the notice
      `ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered that notice of the matter be given
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I be given notice` MEANS
    `s 84 -- notice of the matter must be given to group members` `matter` `damages claimed` `dispensed` `ordered`

@export I did not receive (or did not respond to) a notice in the class action: does that undo a step taken, an order or the judgment (s 85(8))? No.
GIVEN `missed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not receive, or did not respond to, a notice in the class action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does a missed notice undo anything` MEANS
    `s 85(8) -- my not receiving or answering a notice undoes a step, order or judgment` `missed`

@export The defendant has sued me separately in the Supreme Court: can the Court hold back (stay execution of) what I am awarded in the class action (s 81)? Yes, until the defendant's proceeding against you is determined.
GIVEN `sued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant has commenced proceedings in the Supreme Court of Tasmania against you
      `determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those other proceedings have been determined
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my award be stayed` MEANS
    `s 81 -- the Court may stay execution of my award` `sued` `determined`

§§ `Judgment and damages`

-- Arises once the class action reaches judgment or settlement.

@export Can the Court award damages to the group as a lump sum without fixing each member's share (s 86(1)(f), (3))? Only if a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total the group members will be entitled to, except where the award gives effect to a settlement the Court approves under s 82.
GIVEN `settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the award gives effect to a settlement approved by the Court under s 82
      `assessable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total amount the group members will be entitled to
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can damages be awarded as a lump sum` MEANS
    `s 86(3) -- the Court may award aggregate damages` `settlement` `assessable`

@export What is the earliest day the Court can set as the last day for claiming from a damages fund (s 87(3)(c))? The claim day must not be earlier than 6 months after the day the order setting up the fund is made.
GIVEN `order made` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court made the order constituting the fund
GIVETH A DATE
`Earliest claim day for the fund` MEANS
    `s 87(3)(c) -- the earliest claim day the Court may specify` `order made`

@export Is my claim for payment out of the class action fund in time, and if late can it still be allowed (s 87(3)(c), (4))? Claims are due on or before the day the Court specifies; after it the Court may allow a late claim if it is just and the fund has not been fully distributed or paid back to the defendant.
GIVEN `order made` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court made the order constituting the fund
      `claim day` IS A DATE @desc The day the order specifies, on or before which group members are to claim
      `claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made your claim on the fund
      `claimed on` IS A DATE @desc The date you made your claim (if you have not, any date: it is not used)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `fund exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund has already been fully distributed, or paid to the defendant under s 87(5)
      `allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has allowed your late claim as just
GIVETH A `Where my claim on the fund stands`
`Is my claim on the fund in time` MEANS
    `s 87(3)(c), (4) -- where my claim on the fund stands` `order made` `claim day` `claimed` `claimed on` `today` `fund exhausted` `allowed`

@export Am I bound by the judgment in the class action (s 88)? The judgment binds every group member it affects, except a person who opted out under s 71.
GIVEN `opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you opted out of the class action under s 71
      `affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judgment describes or identifies you as one of the group members affected by it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I bound by the judgment` MEANS
    `s 88 -- the judgment binds me` `opted out` `affected`

§§ `Appeals`

-- Arises once judgment is given.

@export The representative party has not appealed in time: what is the last day on which I, as another group member, can appeal for the group (s 89(3))? Within a further 21 days after the time allowed to the representative party ends.
GIVEN `last day for representative` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the time allowed for the representative party (or sub-group representative party) to appeal
GIVETH A DATE
`Last day for my appeal for the group` MEANS
    `s 89(3) -- the last day of the further 21-day period` `last day for representative`

@export Is my appeal for the group in time, or can I still bring one, where the representative party has not appealed (s 89(3))? If the representative party (or sub-group representative party) does not appeal within the time allowed, another member may appeal for the group within a further 21 days.
GIVEN `judgment` IS A DATE @desc The date of the judgment
      `last day for representative` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the time allowed for the representative party to appeal
      `representative appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the representative party appealed within the time allowed
      `appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have instituted an appeal for the group
      `appealed on` IS A DATE @desc The date you instituted it (if you have not, any date: it is not used)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where my appeal for the group stands`
`Is my appeal for the group in time` MEANS
    `s 89(3) -- where my appeal for the group stands` `judgment` `last day for representative` `representative appealed` `appealed` `appealed on` `today`

§§ `Limitation periods`

@export Is the limitation period on my claim running while the class action goes on (s 89B)? It is suspended when the class action begins and runs again only if you opt out, the proceeding is discontinued, or it (with any appeals) ends without finally disposing of your claim; a claim already out of time when it began is not revived.
GIVEN `kind` IS A `Kind of proceeding` @desc What kind of proceeding the class action is: a civil proceeding in the Supreme Court of Tasmania; a criminal proceeding; or a proceeding in another court
      `commenced` IS A DATE @desc The date the class action was commenced
      `limitation last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day on which you could have started your own proceeding under the limitation law, leaving the class action aside
      `happened` IS A `What has happened to the class action` @desc What has happened: it is still running; you opted out; it was discontinued; it and any appeals ended without finally disposing of your claim; it finally disposed of your claim; or the Court ordered it no longer continue as a class action
GIVETH A `My limitation period`
`Is my limitation period running` MEANS
    `s 89B -- my limitation period` (`ss 64, 65 -- Part VII applies to the proceeding` `kind` `commenced`) `commenced` `limitation last day` `happened`

@export If I opt out or the class action ends without deciding my claim, by what date must I start my own proceeding (s 89B)? The days that were left on your limitation period when the class action began start running again from the day you opted out, the discontinuance, or the final determination.
GIVEN `kind` IS A `Kind of proceeding` @desc What kind of proceeding the class action is: a civil proceeding in the Supreme Court of Tasmania; a criminal proceeding; or a proceeding in another court
      `commenced` IS A DATE @desc The date the class action was commenced
      `limitation last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day on which you could have started your own proceeding under the limitation law, leaving the class action aside
      `happened` IS A `What has happened to the class action` @desc What has happened: it is still running; you opted out; it was discontinued; it and any appeals ended without finally disposing of your claim; it finally disposed of your claim; or the Court ordered it no longer continue as a class action
      `happened on` IS A DATE @desc The date it happened: the day you gave your opt-out notice, the day of discontinuance, or the day of the final determination
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I start my own proceeding` MEANS
    `s 89B -- the last day to start my own proceeding` (`ss 64, 65 -- Part VII applies to the proceeding` `kind` `commenced`) `commenced` `limitation last day` `happened` `happened on`
